## Version 8.5.2

- base image upgraded to Ubuntu 26.04 (Python 3.14, GDAL 3.12, PROJ 9.7); all Python packages pinned to their current major versions
- bundled MapServer upgraded to 8.6.6, built with OGC API support; the build tarball is created locally by `install/image.py`
- `Application.register_supported_crs()` lets plugins add a CRS to the raster subsystem; QField projects register their QGIS CRS
- fixed: temporary layers (e.g. QField base maps) had no raster grabbers and rendered nothing
- fixed: features on the edge of a data-derived layer extent were missing from `mapGetFeatures`
- fixed: QField base map rendering failed for paletted images
- fixed: wrong results from `datetimex.difference` with pendulum's compiled extension

## Version 8.5.1

- MapProxy replaced by the built-in raster subsystem: raster layers are fetched, reprojected and cached in-process
- one global tile grid per CRS for all layers and the WMTS service; layer `grid`, `server.mapproxy` and `withMapproxy` are ignored
- `cache.maxLevel` refers to the global grid and defaults to 18; small explicit values need adjusting
- added `cache.name` and `cache.crs` options
- uncached layers keep tiles for 60 seconds, so a viewport is rendered once per block
- raster layers are available in every CRS their extent intersects
- added `display: client` for WMTS layers
- reworked the cache CLI (`gws cache status|seed|drop`)
- HTTP client uses keep-alive connections
- fixed the bbox axis order for box requests in lat/lon maps
- fixed race conditions in directory creation and ephemeral cleanup; file writes are atomic

## Version 8.5.0

- minor bugs fixes and improvements
